ntry></address> </addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADA MITSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address> </addressbook> </applicant> <applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHONO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>EBARA CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HONGO, AKIHISA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MISHIMA, KOJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGATA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SENDAI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, MITSUO</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>CHONO ATSUSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HONGO AKIHISA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MISHIMA KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OGATA AKIRA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SENDAI SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI KENICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TADA MITSUO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>CHONO, ATSUSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HONGO, AKIHISA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MISHIMA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OGATA, AKIRA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SENDAI, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUZUKI, KENICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TADA, MITSUO</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A conduction condition detecting means which can detect a conduction condition (contact condition) of a plurality of feeding contacts in contact with the conduction portion of a substrate to be plated, and a plating device which can form a plating film with a uniform film thickness by uniformizing plating currents flowing through individual feeding contacts. A plating device which plates a substrate to be plated (12), wherein an electrode (13) and a substrate to be plated (12) mounted to a plating jig (11) are arranged opposite to each other in a plating tank (10), the plating jig (11) is provided with a plurality of feeding contact (15) to come into contact with the conduction portion provided on the surface of the substrate to be plated (12), and a specified voltage is applied between the feeding contacts (15) and the electrode (13) to supply a plating current through the feeding contacts (15), the plating device being provided with a conduction condition detecting means (22) for detecting a conduction condition between individual feeding contacts (15) of the plating jig (11) and the conduction portion of the substrate to be plated (12).</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne un moyen de détection d'un état conducteur pouvant détecter un état conducteur (état de contact) d'une pluralité de contacts d'alimentation en contact avec la partie conductrice d'un substrat devant être plaqué, et un dispositif de placage pouvant former un film de placage avec une épaisseur de film uniforme, en uniformisant les courants de placage qui traversent les contacts d'alimentation individuels. Le dispositif de placage plaque un substrat devant être plaqué (12), une électrode (13) et un substrat devant être plaqués (12) sont montés face à face sur un gabarit de placage (11) dans une cuve de placage (10). La cuve de placage (11) est pourvue d'une pluralité de contacts d'alimentation (15) venant en contact avec la partie conductrice située à la surface du substrat devant être plaqué (12). Une tension spécifiée est appliquée entre les contacts d'alimentation (15) et l'électrode (13) de manière à fournir un courant de placage à travers les contacts d'alimentation (15). Le dispositif de placage comprend un moyen de détection (22) d'un état conducteur permettant de détecter un état conducteur entre les contacts d'alimentation individuels (15) de la cuve de placage (11) et la partie conductrice du substrat devant être plaqué (12).</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>